    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green). The only concrete test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and both its cases pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `registrationDate` feature for owner creation on the `POST /api/owners` endpoint.\n\n**Behavior:** When a registration date is supplied it's kept as-is; when omitted it defaults to the server's current date. It's returned as `registrationDate` in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (the default Jackson serialization of `LocalDate`).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, this makes the field both settable on create and returned on read; the OpenAPI generator maps `format: date` to `LocalDate` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date DATE` column, with getter/setter (mirroring `Pet.birthDate`).\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, default `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when none is provided (before saving).\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres` `schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. The tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the schema change is required there.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps `registrationDate` automatically by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.",
